WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.370
- Back in October, we
did a monster of a show.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.900
It was New Kids on the Block,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.660
Salt-N-Pepa, En Vogue and Rick Astley.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.030
It couldn't have been cooler
to have them all here,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.480
as they got ready to kick
off their Mixtape Tour 2022.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.550
But with all that talent,
all those personalities,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.560
we couldn't contain it in an hour.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.030
This was a lot of people talking, right?

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.700
So check out what we
couldn't share until now.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.690
Jordan.
- Yes?

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.554
- Who would win in a dance
battle today? I'm just curious.

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:29.554
- I honestly believe we
all have our own moves

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.254
that, like, one person-

00:00:31.254 --> 00:00:32.460
- Oh, you're a politician.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:33.293
You're the politician of the group.

00:00:33.293 --> 00:00:34.200
(all laughing)
- No, no. I'm serious.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.969
- It's how we've stayed
together for 30 years.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.020
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.310
- No, I'm serious, like-

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.630
- [Kelly] Well, you were the
one dancing in the break,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.530
is all I'm saying.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.631
- Oh, yeah. True.
(all laughing)

00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:46.920
I just like to dance.
We all like to dance.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.410
- I love that. I do,
I really can't express

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.243
how cool that is.

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:51.810
Not a lot of people have

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.460
that kind of group around you,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.096
or love around you for your whole life.

00:00:56.096 --> 00:00:57.997
Especially being in the limelight.

00:00:57.997 --> 00:00:58.830
(audience clapping, cheering)

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.203
Like, having that trust?

00:01:00.203 --> 00:01:03.990
- A lot of bands don't benefit
from the history they have

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.240
for, you know, a lot of
reasons bands break up.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.030
But we have that gift that we were,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.380
we did take some time off.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.410
But now, you know, to
share that with our fans

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.150
and embrace it with the history

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.820
and a different perspective is, it's like,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:18.900
such a bonus.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.100
- Especially for people
in the limelight, though,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.570
it's hard to trust people sometimes

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.370
and know why they're here, you know?

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.930
Like around you. So that's cool.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.310
- We've always kept each other in line.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.143
I mean, that was one thing.

00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:29.070
When we got successful at
an early age, it was like,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.720
if somebody pulled up in a Ferrari,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.633
the other guys would be
like, "What's wrong with you?

00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:34.170
You grew up taking the subway,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.880
what are you doing
driving a Ferrari?" But-

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.041
- And then you ask to drive it?

00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:37.982
(all laughing)

00:01:37.982 --> 00:01:39.990
- No, no. We really, I mean,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.496
- Then you're like, can
I take it for a spin?

00:01:41.496 --> 00:01:42.329
- Where's ours? Yeah.

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:44.520
- We kept it pretty
simple and I think that's,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.452
we attribute that to having
each other, you know?

00:01:46.452 --> 00:01:48.180
- Oh that's really cool.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.520
So did y'all also know that you had a gift

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.470
for harmony and singing
whenever you were young?

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.550
- I didn't even know I could sing.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.630
I think it was about the age of 12,

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.240
- I was 13!
- Really?

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.770
- Yeah! People think it's
when you're so young!

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.910
No. It was 13.
- Exactly.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.520
I was sitting on the
floor looking at cartoons

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.110
and my sisters were on the sofa,

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.170
and I just started humming the cartoon.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.600
And my sister said, "Terry! You can sing!"

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.834
And I was like, "Oh. Okay."

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:13.290
(all laughing)

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.620
After that, she had me practicing
after school every day.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.030
- Oh, I love that!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.260
She was like, "you get to work." (laughs)

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.270
- You're gonna sing girl.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.590
- I grew up in church singing,

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.240
so everyone sang.
- Right.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.470
- So, it wasn't so normal.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.760
Like, everyone around me sang,

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.960
that's why I feel like I wasn't,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.460
I didn't really know
until I was, like, 13.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.470
I was like, "Oh, wait, maybe
I can do something with this."

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.580
That's cool.
- Mm. Yeah.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.630
- Yeah, what about you, Rhona?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.060
- It's the same way I discovered
harmonizing, was in church.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.890
And singing with the traveling choir,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.620
Soul Children of Chicago, shout out to my

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.670
Soul Children alumni.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.980
- It's such a beautiful way
to learn how to sing, too.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.060
'Cause you're not thinking about it,

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.020
and you're just, you know,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.940
you're thinking about
something other than yourself.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.773
I love that.

00:02:48.773 --> 00:02:50.430
A lot of my friends, that's
how we all grew up singing,

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.480
was in church.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.650
But it's kinda tricky though,

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.483
'cause everybody's like,

00:02:53.483 --> 00:02:54.390
"Oh my gosh, you're such a great singer."

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.223
And I'm like, "you should hear the people

00:02:55.223 --> 00:02:56.760
I grew up singing with." (laughs)

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.593
- Right.

00:02:57.593 --> 00:02:59.010
- I grew up singing with some
pretty great singers, so.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.930
Were you always Salt-N-Pepa
or did you have a different,

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.460
I heard you had a different name at first.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.840
- Yeah.
- Super Nature.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.800
- Oh my gosh.
(imitates fireworks exploding)

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.943
- That wouldn't have worked, right?

00:03:05.943 --> 00:03:08.040
- Can you imagine?
- Nah.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.540
- Super Nature is my favorite thing

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.507
I've learned about y'all.

00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:11.610
(Kelly laughing)
- That's crazy.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.443
- It was so formal.

00:03:12.443 --> 00:03:13.800
- Who came up with Super Nature?

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.820
- [Both] Hurby.
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.980
- And then the fans kinda named us.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.367
Because we, in a rap, said,

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.480
"We go together like salt
and pepper" and so it stuck.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.770
And it was like, that works!

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.990
- Play that song from them
salt and pepper girls.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.160
- That's what they used to say

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.390
on the radio all the time.
- Them salt and pepper girls.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.920
- Oh my gosh, give it up to the fans.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.300
- Yes.
- Well that worked out.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.728
- Give it up to the fans!
- Yes!

00:03:31.728 --> 00:03:33.377
(all clapping, cheering)

00:03:33.377 --> 00:03:36.630
So you guys all had pretty iconic looks,

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.800
everybody up here, back in the day.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.230
But here are some I wanna show.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.253
So, Danny,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.470
this is great.
- Aww.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.910
- Wow.
- Look at you! How cute.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.020
Look, I dressed today to try
and fit in with these. (laughs)

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.910
But Danny, are there any
looks that you'd prefer

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.410
never to see again?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.243
Just curious.

00:03:53.243 --> 00:03:54.630
- [Danny] I mean, I
didn't mind that last one.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.370
This one's okay. We look all right.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.670
- [Kelly] Yeah! I think
you look cool as hell!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.589
I have a ton I wish I'd never done!

00:04:01.589 --> 00:04:03.060
(all laughing)

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.920
Geez, I'm like what?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.643
That's so awesome! I mean, so much style!

00:04:07.643 --> 00:04:09.757
- [Danny] That's when we
were chasing Salt-N-Pepa.

00:04:09.757 --> 00:04:11.010
(all laughing)

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.539
- [Kelly] I love that, you were on top.

00:04:12.539 --> 00:04:14.264
(scattered chatter)

00:04:14.264 --> 00:04:16.011
- Okay, so what,
- We were wearing our merch.

00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:18.150
(Salt-N-Pepa laughing)

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.140
Oh, my God! Do you ever,

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.310
okay, do you do that though?

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.480
Because I sometimes, like,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.770
I have this song called "Love So Soft"

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:23.640
and there's a sweatshirt of mine,

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.440
and they made it really soft.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.870
And I just really love
wearing it because it's soft,

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.190
but I have to, like,
wear it around my house.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.023
'Cause I'm like,

00:04:30.023 --> 00:04:31.890
"what am I gonna show
up with my name on me?"

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:32.850
- Right, right.
- And maybe I will!

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:36.180
- Maybe I will.
- Yeah, why not? Why not?

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.123
- Yeah.
- I always wonder 'bout that.

00:04:38.123 --> 00:04:41.163
(audience clapping)
I love how soft it is!

